// expect: 30
// mn-multishot — STEP 3 / W07 gate: the MULTI-SHOT PRODUCER + LIVE CAPTURES.
//
// A handler arm with TWO sequential (non-disjoint) resume sites classifies
// MultiShot (infer_resume_cardinality: multiple sites, not branch-disjoint).
// The continuation must be reified (LMakeContinuation) and CALLED TWICE — the
// arm resumes once with 10, once with 20; the body after `pick()` returns its
// input and the handler sums the two runs: 10 + 20 = 30, NOT the one-shot 10.
// Proves the producer mints the heap record and the catching handler re-enters
// it a second time.
//
// W07 — REAL CAPTURES: the arm sums `a + b`, the two arm-frame locals bound by
// the two resumptions. With the live-capture lowering, the continuation record
// captures EXACTLY the free vars the resumption body reads (the same
// collect_free_vars/resolve_captures_outer the closure path uses — handler =
// state = closure = continuation, ONE capture mechanism). The former `[]`
// captures left a resumed body reading garbage; the real set makes `a + b` read
// the actual 10 and 20.
//
// LAW 7: the OneShot path (every ev*/eq micro) stays byte-identical — this is
// an ADDED form, not a perturbation. The MultiShot producer fires ONLY for an
// arm the body proves multi-shot.
//
// SEED PEER: the seed's WAT (bootstrap/src/lower/*, tag 312 arity-6) lags the
// 7-field record + live-capture reification — it still resolves resume one-shot
// (exit 10, not 30). Named positive-form peer Hβ.seed.multishot-capture: the
// seed catches up to the .mn-led continuation-reification codegen. The .mn
// leads; this micro is the structural gate the seed will satisfy at first-light.
//
// Run: tools/run-micro.sh tests/micros/mn-multishot.mn 30
// Expected exit 30: total = run(10) + run(20) = 10 + 20.

effect Pick { pick() -> Int }

// Two resume sites, sequential in the arm body → MultiShot. Each resume runs
// the continuation (the rest of `body`, which returns its input) and the arm
// sums the two resumptions' results.
handler twice with total = 0 {
  pick() => {
    let a = resume(10)
    let b = resume(20)
    a + b
  }
}

fn body() = pick()

fn main(q) = { body() } ~> twice
